---
# [Model storage setup]($heading.id('model-storage-setup'))

Use `hf://org/repo` for Hugging Face. Omit the revision to use `main`, or add
`@revision` to select one. Use `s3://` or `gs://` for object storage.

- **S3** · Use a local copy of the model when your setup requires an AWS session token.
- **Google Cloud Storage** · The reviewed loader supports authorized-user
  application default credentials and GCE metadata. It does not support
  service account key refresh.

See the pinned loaders for
[Hugging Face](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/vfs/hf.zig),
[S3](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/vfs/s3.zig),
and [GCS](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/vfs/gcs.zig).

## [Gated model access]($heading.id('gated-model-access'))

Request access on the Hugging Face model page and use a read token from
the approved account. Export `HF_TOKEN` or sign in with
`uvx --from huggingface_hub hf auth login` for a host download.

